# Workspace container assets must keep LF endings.
#
# These shell scripts are bind-mounted into Linux containers by the generated
# workspace compose files (db-init for PostgreSQL/Keycloak, the MinIO
# entrypoint). The repository stores them with LF, but with core.autocrlf=true
# a Windows checkout rewrites them to CRLF and the container fails to execute
# them:
#
#   /scripts/init-database.sh: line 2: : not found
#   /scripts/init-database.sh: set: line 3: illegal option -
#
# which makes the *-db-prepare services exit 2 and leaves Keycloak unable to
# start. Pinning the eol here keeps the checked-out copy executable.
docker/**/*.sh text eol=lf
